  "title": "2.2 Compact Sets",
  "lang": "en",
  "description": "We now consider how a collection of open sets can cover a set $A$ as a whole. Such a collection may contain infinitely many sets, and this raises a natural question. Can finitely many members of the collection already cover $A$? Compactness formalizes the sets for which the answer is always yes.",
